// | `urn:proreta:problem:invalid-credentials` | 401 | Wrong login or password (always the same answer) |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:csrf` | 403 | Missing or wrong `X-CSRF-Token` |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:forbidden` | 403 | The role (in the organization or the project) or the platform-admin flag does not allow the operation |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:account-suspended` | 403 | The organization was suspended or deleted by the platform admin |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:password-change-required` | 403 | The password was issued by somebody else and must be changed first (`mustChangePassword` of the session); only `GET /auth/me`, `POST /auth/logout` and `POST /auth/password` work until then |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:registration-disabled` | 403 | Self-service registration is turned off |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:password-login-disabled` | 403 | Password sign-in is turned off for this user |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:domain-not-verified` | 403 | The sign-in domain was not proven by a recent Google Workspace sign-in |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:domain-not-allowed` | 403 | The operator does not allow claiming this sign-in domain |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:feature-unavailable` | 403 | The organization is not entitled to the feature the operation needs (see `features` of the session) |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:not-found` | 404 | The resource does not exist, was deleted, or the caller does not see it |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:invitation-invalid` | 404 | The invitation token is unknown, expired, used or revoked |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:method-not-allowed` | 405 | The path exists, the method does not |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:not-a-heartbeat` | 409 | The operation exists only for heartbeat monitors |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:email-taken` | 409 | The email is already registered |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:email-settings-conflict` | 409 | The email settings do not allow this now: no server configured, no successful test of the current settings, or a test already pending |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:plan-limit-reached` | 409 | The plan allows no more of a resource; carries `limit` and `max` |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:protected-organization` | 409 | The default organization, or the admin's own, cannot be suspended or deleted |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:organization-deleted` | 409 | A deleted organization cannot be changed |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:system-admin` | 409 | The platform admin's membership cannot be changed through the API, nor its password reset by another admin |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:invitation-accepted` | 409 | The invitation was already used |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:already-member` | 409 | The user is already a member of the organization |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:last-owner` | 409 | The organization would be left without an owner |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:slug-taken` | 409 | The slug of a project or status page is in use |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:project-not-empty` | 409 | The project still has monitors or channels |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:default-project` | 409 | The Default project cannot be deleted |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:no-password` | 409 | The user has no password to change (signed in only with a provider) |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:last-login-method` | 409 | Unlinking would leave the user without a way to sign in |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:domain-taken` | 409 | Another organization claimed the sign-in domain |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:validation` | 422 | A well-formed request breaks a business rule; see `fieldErrors` |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:rate-limited` | 429 | Too many attempts; see `Retry-After` |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:internal` | 500 | Unexpected server error; quote `requestId` when reporting it |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:internal` | 499 | The client cancelled the request; recorded by the server only, never delivered (see the introduction) |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:channel-delivery-failed` | 502 | The notification channel's service did not accept the test message |
// | `urn:proreta:problem:unavailable` | 503 | A dependency (a sign-in provider, the probe location) is temporarily unavailable |
//
// Example: urn:proreta:problem:unauthenticated
type ProblemType = string

